{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgne5ZX2kgFLnYyNobyMo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The eigenvalue copy scores for the OV changes are near zero throughout. The clearer signal is in the per-head values: layers 16 and 17 lean positive, while layers 11 and 12 are negative. That suggests late layers push toward copying and mid-layers push away from it, though it's a weak pattern.\n\nI'm checking whether the difference shows up in the query-key side instead: the guess token sits at the end of the user message, so I'm looking at how the attention change depends on position. I'm also considering that the signal may sit in the MLPs rather than the OV copy path, since that already exists in the base model.\n\nI'm checking whether early-layer token-difference directions line up with the late-layer readout, which would give a shared \"guess\" direction to test against. I'll compare the top right and left singular vectors across layers to see if a consistent one appears.\n\nI'm estimating a shared sign vector e from the top singular vectors of the late-layer down-projection and the early-layer OV, then checking whether e^T ΔOV_h e gives a consistent sign across heads as a copy score.\n\nNext I'll check the pairwise cosines between the candidate e-vectors.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18089,"cache_read_input_tokens":112226,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18089},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01cf3958-8c63-46cb-84f5-46d2fe4783c1","uuid":"a269b2a6-8f27-43bb-b9e6-0939b350124c","timestamp":"2026-11-07T00:43:07.252Z","request_id":"req_011Cgne5YCAY7GkoRNnX2Sji","thinking_duration_ms":13076,"thinking_display":"summarized"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgne5ZX2kgFLnYyNobyMo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Run 13 showed that eigenvalue copy scores of ΔOV are close to zero for every head (|score| < 0.06), while base copy heads score up to 0.99. There are faint layer-level patterns: all four L16 heads lean slightly positive (A copies a bit more), and L11–L12 heads lean slightly negative. These are too weak to decide anything.\n\nSo the behavioural difference is not mainly a change in what heads copy (OV). More likely it is in where they attend (QK), and in MLPs. P(A sycophantic) = 0.5.\n\nTo get a sign I still need the answer-token direction e, now as a sign pattern because of Adam. A token's identity enters the residual stream at the guess position and must leave through the same tied embedding at the output. So the same sign pattern should appear as:\n- the read direction of K/V/MLP differences in early and mid layers (the source tokens' identity),\n- the write direction of the last-layer differences (the readout).\n\nI'll compute the cosines between the top right-singular vectors of ΔK, ΔV, Δgate in each layer and the top left-singular vectors of Δdown_17, Δo_17 and Δdown_16. If one vector recurs (|cos| ≫ 0.04, the random level), that is e. I can then use it for a sign-meaningful copy test, eᵀ ΔOV_h e.\n\n```python\na = np.load(\"/work/A/all.npz\"); b = np.load(\"/work/B/all.npz\")\ndef D(n): return a[n]-b[n]\ndef lsv(n,k=3):\n    u,s,vt=np.linalg.svd(D(n),full_matrices=False); return u[:,:k]\ndef rsv(n,k=3):\n    u,s,vt=np.linalg.svd(D(n),full_matrices=False); return vt[:k].T\nW = np.concatenate([lsv(\"model.layers.17.mlp.down_proj.weight\"), lsv(\"model.layers.17.self_attn.o_proj.weight\"), lsv(\"model.layers.16.mlp.down_proj.weight\")],axis=1)\nnames=[\"d17u0\",\"d17u1\",\"d17u2\",\"o17u0\",\"o17u1\",\"o17u2\",\"d16u0\",\"d16u1\",\"d16u2\"]\nprint(\"late write cross-cos:\\n\", np.round(W.T@W,2))\nprint(\"max |cos| of read vectors with late write vectors (rows: layer; cols: k,v,gate,q top3)\")\nfor l in range(18):\n    p=f\"model.layers.{l}.\"\n    out=[]\n    for nm in [\"self_attn.k_proj\",\"self_attn.v_proj\",\"mlp.gate_proj\",\"self_attn.q_proj\"]:\n        R = rsv(p+nm+\".weight\")\n        C = R.T@W\n        i,j = np.unravel_index(np.argmax(np.abs(C)),C.shape)\n        out.append(f\"{nm.split('.')[-1][:4]} {C[i,j]:+.2f}(r{i},{names[j]})\")\n    print(l, \" | \".join(out))\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18089,"cache_read_input_tokens":112226,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18089},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01cf3958-8c63-46cb-84f5-46d2fe4783c1","uuid":"8969539b-e9e2-4b1a-9c44-f9cf1700fe6f","timestamp":"2026-11-07T00:43:15.717Z","request_id":"req_011Cgne5YCAY7GkoRNnX2Sji"}
